# Make-Ahead Mashed Potatoes (Fridge or Freezer)

Creamy mashed potatoes designed for Sunday prep and easy reheating during the week.

## Ingredients
- 3 lbs Yukon Gold or Russet potatoes
- 6 tbsp butter
- 1 cup heavy cream or half-and-half
- 1/4 cup sour cream (optional)
- 1 tsp salt
- 1/2 tsp black pepper

## Instructions
1. Peel and cut potatoes into chunks.
2. Boil until fork-tender, about 15 minutes.
3. Drain well.
4. Mash potatoes with butter, cream, sour cream (optional), salt, and pepper.
5. Adjust consistency with additional cream as needed.

## Storage
### Refrigeration
- Store up to 4–5 days.
- Press plastic wrap directly onto the surface before sealing.

### Freezer
- Portion into freezer bags.
- Flatten and freeze up to 2 months.

## Reheating
### Microwave
- Add 1–2 tbsp cream or milk.
- Cover and heat 60–90 seconds.
- Stir and continue heating until creamy.

### Ninja Foodi
- Steam 3–5 minutes, or
- Sauté on low with a splash of cream.

### Oven
- Bake at 350°F, covered, for 20–25 minutes.

## Servings
Makes 6–8 servings.
